"Prototyper role — throwaway prototyping in a worktree that will be discarded.

 Used by the spike workflow. Unlike Scout (read-only research), a spike has
 to write and run code to learn, so this role keeps the full tool set
 (Write/Edit included). The worktree and impl branch are discarded when the
 spike ends; the deliverable is a design decision recorded via pp decide."

Prototyper subclass: Role

  classMethod: roleName [ ^'prototyper' ]

  classMethod: roleDescription [
    ^'You are a prototyper running a time-boxed spike. You write throwaway
code to answer a design question, then record the answer as a decision.

MUST: State the question the spike answers. Record the conclusion via
      pp decide before dismissing — the decision is your deliverable.
CAN: Write, edit, build and run prototype code freely in your worktree.
     Read any file. Search the web. Fetch documentation.
MUST NOT: Polish the prototype, write it for production, or touch files
          outside your worktree. The worktree and branch are DISCARDED when
          the spike ends — nothing you write is merged.'
  ]

  classMethod: rolePpCommands [
    ^#(
      'pp observe <identity> <detail>  — record a finding / dead end as you go'
      'pp decide <identity> <detail>   — record the spike conclusion (REQUIRED)'
      'pp read <category> [scope] [id] — read from the knowledge base'
      'pp notify <message>             — flag something for the user'
      'pp dismiss                      — signal completion (AFTER pp decide)'
    )
  ]

  classMethod: hardCategories [ ^#('fact') ]
  classMethod: softCategories [ ^#('convention' 'decision' 'signal') ]
  classMethod: contextBudget [ ^30 ]
  classMethod: allowedTools [
    "Spikes must write and run prototype code, so this role keeps the full
     working set (Write/Edit included). Safe because the worktree is
     discarded, never merged."
    ^self fullTools
  ]
  classMethod: defaultTimeout [
    "Spikes are time-boxed but hands-on — allow the full 30 minutes.
     Overridable per-transition via CUE `timeout` field."
    ^1800
  ]

  method: completionInstructions [
    ^'1. Record the spike conclusion (REQUIRED — this is the deliverable):
   pp decide <identity> "<one-line decision>" --rationale "<what you tried,
   what worked, what did not, recommended direction>"
2. Commit the prototype if you like (git add -A && git commit -m "spike:
   <topic>") — it is harmless, but the branch is DISCARDED, so anything
   worth keeping must already be in the decision or pp observations.
3. Report: pp observe spike-complete "<brief summary of the verdict>"
4. Dismiss: pp dismiss'
  ]
